<p>France moved the aircraft carrier Charles de Gaulle and its strike group through the Suez Canal toward the southern Red Sea on Wednesday, pre-positioning the force for a possible French-British mission to secure shipping in the Strait of Hormuz, French officials said. The French Armed Forces Ministry said the move was designed to shorten the time needed to launch the initiative if conditions allow, while officials described the proposed operation as defensive and separate from current military operations in the region. The deployment follows weeks of planning by France and Britain for a multinational effort to restore freedom of navigation after traffic through the waterway, which normally carries about one-fifth of global crude oil, was largely halted during the conflict involving the United States, Israel and Iran that began on Feb. 28. Macron said on X that he had told Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian of his deep concern over escalation in the Gulf region as peace talks stalled.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/YJ7Ue1L-g9R7oQ3DAcBOD7EUGBVGIWPjBXpbikwWhTDvzpyaDHNvOvVwnW3pErXTs2eXA9eyVdhVu5q7JqM7qz9B3n0pOeQQZTYNXpMdz9Ra6U5aVSlqYsGVCERDBFbnNnMOEgrPmRkC7vh6Mxb39EHJuHsUI5_y12k' alt='France&#x27;s nuclear-powered aircraft carrier Charles de Gaulle is seen at Souda Bay in Crete, Greece, on April 7, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Coalition scale: Reports put the planning group at more than 40 countries, while Politico said the April initiative gathered 51 countries.</li><li>Escorts included: The French carrier group was accompanied by Italian and Dutch warships as it headed toward the southern Red Sea, according to accounts citing French officials.</li><li>Recent clashes: Fresh exchanges of fire on Monday increased concern over the four-week-old U.S.-Iran truce and rival maritime blockades around the strait, Reuters reported.</li></ul><blockquote>All parties must lift the blockade of the strait, without delay and without conditions, - Emmanuel Macron</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>French military: The deployment aims to assess the operational environment, expand crisis-management options and support integration of partner nations&#x27; assets under international law. (<a href='https://humenglish.com/latest/france-deploys-aircraft-carrier-to-red-sea-amid-hormuz-security-push/'>HumEnglish</a>)</li><li>French presidency official: An official in Macron&#x27;s office said the continuing blockade was inflicting growing damage on the world economy and that prolonged hostilities were too serious a risk to accept. (<a href='https://minutemirror.com.pk/france-deploys-aircraft-carrier-to-red-sea-in-push-to-open-strait-of-hormuz-551703/'>Minute Mirror</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/05/france-moves-aircraft-carrier-red-sea-eye-hormuz-mission'>France moves aircraft carrier to Red Sea with eye on Hormuz mission</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/french-carrier-group-moves-south-suez-ahead-conditional-132708522'>French carrier group moves south of Suez ahead of conditional UK-French Hormuz mission</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-france-moves-aircraft-carrier-group-toward-strait-of-hormuz-for/'>France moves aircraft carrier group toward Strait of Hormuz for possible defensive mission</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/france-moves-aircraft-carrier-to-red-sea-with-eye-on-hormuz-mission'>France moves aircraft carrier to Red Sea with eye on Strait of Hormuz mission</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1998259/france-sends-aircraft-carrier-to-middle-east-for-possible-hormuz-mission'>France sends aircraft carrier to Middle East for possible Hormuz mission</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://apnews.com/article/french-carrier-charles-de-gaulle-suez-hormuz-2749dc877f0ac34a0ccd4f0530786009